.TH ESHEEP 1 "August 2026" "linux-esheep 0.1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
esheep \- a small animated desktop sheep
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B esheep
.RI [ options ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
eSheep walks across the monitor workarea and, on X11, can land on visible
application windows and panels. Left-click and drag moves the sheep. A
double-click makes it jump. Right-click opens the quit menu.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B --help
Show command-line help.
.TP
.B --version
Show the program version.
.TP
.BI --sprite\  PATH
Use the specified spritesheet.
.TP
.BI --spawn\  MODE
Use \fBbottom\fR (default), \fBwindow\fR, or \fBrandom\fR startup placement.
.TP
.B --no-window-landing
Disable X11 window and panel detection.
.TP
.B --allow-conky
Allow Conky windows as landing surfaces.
.TP
.BI --tick-ms\  N
Set the update interval from 10 to 1000 milliseconds.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B ESHEEP_SPRITESHEET
Default spritesheet path.
.TP
.B ESHEEP_TICK_MS
Default update interval.
.TP
.B ESHEEP_WINDOW_LANDING
Set to 0 to disable X11 landing.
.TP
.B ESHEEP_EXCLUDE_CONKY
Set to 0 to allow Conky landing.
.TP
.B ESHEEP_SPAWN
Set to \fBwindow\fR to start on an application window.
.SH NOTES
Window discovery is available on X11. On Wayland, the sheep retains monitor
bottom movement and dragging without application-window discovery.
